ts of a feeding, then check what Luther says about helping people in need.","finding":"ML1027"},{"world":"divinity-light-reading-scenes-v4","collection":"items","owner":"road-panel","field":"reading.text","before":"The Samaritan helps across a religious boundary, while Jewish Scripture already teaches care for strangers. These points do not require portraying Judaism as lacking mercy or as a failed version of Christianity.","after":"The Samaritan helps across a religious boundary. Jewish Scripture already teaches care for strangers.","finding":"ML1053"},{"world":"divinity-light-reading-scenes-v4","collection":"items","owner":"road-panel","field":"description","before":"The Samaritan helps across a religious boundary, while Jewish Scripture already teaches care for strangers. These points do not require portraying Judaism as lacking mercy or as a failed version of Christianity.","after":"The Samaritan helps across a religious boundary. Jewish Scripture already teaches care for strangers.","finding":"ML1053-matching-description"},{"world":"divinity-light-reading-scenes-v4","collection":"items","owner":"jewish-mercy","field":"reading.text","before":"The Gospel’s discussion of neighbor-love does not start from a Judaism without mercy. The Leviticus passage already connects love of the stranger with Israel’s memory of being foreigners.","after":"Leviticus connects love of strangers with Israel’s memory of being foreigners. Jesus and the lawyer discuss neighbour-love within that Jewish tradition.","finding":"ML1051"},{"world":"mars-purposeful-fieldwork-v8","collection":"chapters","owner":"outcrop","field":"completionText","before":"The ice sample is labelled, and the photographs record the specimen and cliff layers. These observations do not yet establish how old the layers are or how they formed.","after":"The ice sample is labelled, and the photographs record the specimen and the core’s layers. These observations do not yet establish how old the layers are or how they f