ass needle turn. This shows that electricity can have a magnetic effect without a visible mechanical push.","finding":"I10"},{"world":"atlas-focused-sessions-v6","collection":"milestones","owner":"plain-atlas-frame-dependent-simultaneity","field":"text","before":"The flashes are simultaneous in the platform frame. In the train frame, equal paths and the same light speed mean their different arrival times imply different emission times. The disagreement concerns simultaneity after accounting for travel time, not just a delayed signal.","after":"Two flashes happen at a moving train's ends at the same time according to platform clocks, but their light reaches a passenger at the train's midpoint at different times. For the passenger, light travels equal distances from the two ends at the same speed. The passenger therefore concludes that the flashes happened at different times.","finding":"I11a"},{"world":"atlas-focused-sessions-v6","collection":"items","owner":"special-relativity","field":"reading.text","before":"Observers moving steadily relative to one another use the same physical laws but need not agree on distant simultaneity. Newton's mechanics remains a useful approximation in everyday conditions.","after":"Observers moving steadily past one another use the same physical laws and measure the same speed of light. They can still disagree about whether far-apart events happened at the same time. Newton's mechanics remains a useful approximation at everyday speeds.","finding":"I11b"},{"world":"atlas-focused-sessions-v6","collection":"items","owner":"special-relativity","field":"description","before":"Observers moving steadily relative to one another use the same physical laws but need not agree on distant simultaneity. Newton's mechanics remains a useful approximation in everyday conditions.","after":"Observers moving steadily past one another use the same physical laws and measure the same speed of light. They can still disagree about whether far-apart events happe